  "scope": "Reanalysis of preserved captures; no new board run, hardware modification or timing work.",
  "findings": [
    "RX contiguous prefix assembly adds two FSM states on the metadata-only short RPC path; descriptor-to-app-response median increases 15 ns, descriptor-to-sys-response mean increases 10.45 ns.",
    "Inline TX restore waits for packet RAM write response before descriptor submission: invalidation completion to submission grows 15 to 45 ns median.",
    "Old 8-byte RPC reply has DmaLength=0 and TxNoDmaRead; current reply has DmaLength=8 and TxAfterDmaRead. Net submit-to-MAC grows 155 to 165 ns median; overlapping encoder stages must not be summed as an independent DMA duration.",
    "DCS TX ingress grows 205 to 215 ns median. In the representative pair, R12/s1__3pRA3/RDD is identical, sys request to DCS RDD is 125 ns in both, and RDD-to-commit is 80 vs 90 ns. The endpoint read FSM and interface routing source have no corresponding added state; the remaining two-cycle cause is not proven by these trace points.",
    "Control forward/ack median remains 245 ns. No extra control/overflow transaction occurs between RX response and TX request in the representative pair. The 401.845 ns mean growth in that interval is host/link turnaround, not evidence of a 402 ns FPGA processing regression."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Separate historical cohorts and boots, not a controlled same-software bitstream A/B.",
    "5 ns trace quantization and app/sys crossing observation uncertainty apply; source pipeline delays are corrected with each matching map.",
    "Control invalidation interval includes coherent CPU response, not exclusively FPGA combinational logic.",
    "No CPU-only or pure-wire attribution of the host-turnaround delta; old CPU epoch fit is not used.",
    "No claimed exact RTL root cause for the small DCS RDD-to-commit increase.",
    "No new timing-closure claim."
  ],
